---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';
const path = '/use-cases/black-friday';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/black-friday');
const desc = description(site, 'use-cases/black-friday');
const comparisonApps = [
  'sequenzy', 'klaviyo', 'omnisend', 'privy', 'postscript', 'drip',
  'yotpo-email-sms', 'sendlane', 'firepush', 'attentive',
].map((s) => appBySlug(s)!).filter(Boolean);
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<article class="container prose-shopify py-16">
<a href="/use-cases">All use cases</a>
<h1>Black Friday SMS campaign operations</h1>
<p>Plan Cyber Week as one campaign calendar across email, SMS, and existing automations. A sale broadcast, cart reminder, and VIP announcement can compete for the same customer. The workflow below is a proposed operating plan, not a report of merchant tests or guaranteed revenue.</p>
<h2>Build a sale control sheet</h2><p>For each offer record the owner, eligible market, start and end timezone, stock scope, destination URL, discount rules, and last safe dispatch time. Include scheduled campaigns and triggered flows. Freeze ordinary edits at a date the team can support; keep a named operator able to cancel queued sends if price or inventory changes.</p>
<h2>Separate access from eligibility</h2><p>VIP early access needs an explicit audience snapshot and a working restricted destination if access is actually exclusive. A private-looking link alone is not a gate. Decide whether newly qualified customers join after the snapshot and what happens when a shared link reaches a nonmember. Keep the public launch audience separate so VIPs do not receive a redundant announcement.</p>
<h2>Resolve collisions before the sale opens</h2><p>Choose which message wins when a subscriber is waiting in cart recovery and a sale starts. Recheck purchase status and channel permission before dispatch, rather than relying only on the original audience export. Suppress a reminder for an already purchased item; a different-category offer needs its own relevance decision. Document the frequency policy across campaigns and flows, including what the tooling cannot enforce centrally.</p>
<h2>Rehearse failures with test profiles</h2><p>Proposed checks: purchase between scheduling and sending; unsubscribe after joining the VIP list; sell out the advertised variant; extend the sale; end it while a queued reminder waits. Check destination price, market currency, automatic discounts, and fulfillment promises. A sale extension must update the landing page and queued copy together. Do not send a false last-chance message just because an old timer expired.</p>
<h2>Budget for a stop, not only a launch</h2><p>Estimate eligible SMS recipients, message segments, destination rates, and fees using the supplier's current quote. Assign someone to monitor spend, replies, complaints, failed sends, and stock during the event. Agree on conditions to pause and investigate. A universal daily cadence or fixed recovery pause is not a substitute for those observations.</p>
<h2>Close the event cleanly</h2><p>Expire obsolete creative and reconcile purchase suppression before Cyber Monday follow-ups. Separate gift purchases from self-purchases when planning later messages. Review contribution after returns and incentives, not only attributed sale revenue. Compare audience composition and offer depth before interpreting year-over-year changes; January weakness alone cannot diagnose reputation damage.</p>
<p>Use <a href="/use-cases/discount-strategy">discount strategy</a> for combination and margin checks, and <a href="/use-cases/deliverability">deliverability</a> for sender diagnostics. This calendar coordinates those controls; it does not replace them.</p>
<h2>App discovery and demonstration checklist</h2>
<p>Use these profiles as starting points. Ask each supplier to demonstrate this workflow with your events, markets, permissions, and failure cases before buying. Listing is not a verified feature comparison or performance ranking; confirm current plans and destination charges directly.</p>
<ul>{comparisonApps.map(app => <li><a href={`/apps/${app.slug}`}>{app.name}</a></li>)}</ul>
</article>
</BaseLayout>
